+<intent-contract>
+
+## Intent
+
+**Problem:** CI logs are verbose—the full frai-gate report takes many lines. Teams need a compact one-liner to scan gate status in CI output.
+
+**Approach:** Add a `renderSummary()` function that formats gate results as `<VERDICT> <answered>/<total>` with block-causing checks listed inline, and expose it via a `--summary` flag on the `frai-gate check` command.
+
+## Boundaries & Constraints
+
+**Always:**
+- Total checks is always 7 (the length of GATE_CHECKS).
+- Answered count = number of checks with no 'block' severity finding (warnings do not reduce answered).
+- Block check IDs appear in the order defined by GATE_CHECKS (not alphabetical or frequency order).
+- Special case: if the gate section itself is missing (a 'structure' finding exists), return `BLOCK 0/7: structure` and no other check IDs.
+- `--json` flag takes priority if both `--json` and `--summary` are passed.
+- Exit codes unchanged: 1 on BLOCK, 0 otherwise.
+
+**Never:**
+- Do not count warnings toward answered checks or include warning-only checks in the summary output.
+- Do not reorder or deduplicate check IDs — emit each once in schema order.
+- Do not include the verdict icon (✅, ⚠️, ⛔) in the summary output.
+
+## I/O & Edge-Case Matrix
+
+| Scenario | Input / State | Expected Output | Error Handling |
+|----------|--------------|-----------------|----------------|
+| All passed | No findings | `PASS 7/7` | No error |
+| Some answered | 2 findings (evaluation, transparency) w/ block severity | `BLOCK 5/7: evaluation, transparency` | No error |
+| Structure missing | gateSection is null, 'structure' finding present | `BLOCK 0/7: structure` | No error |
+| Warnings only | 3 warn findings (no block) | `WARN 7/7` | No error |
+| Check `--summary` + `--json` | Both flags passed | Uses `--json` output (full JSON), not summary | No error |
+| Check `--summary` without gate section | No gate section, no structure finding | `PASS 0/7` (no findings → verdict=PASS, no blocks) | No error |
+
+</intent-contract>
+
+## Code Map
+
+- `packages/frai-gate/src/gate/schema.ts` — Defines GATE_CHECKS (7 checks), GateResult, Finding, and Verdict types.
+- `packages/frai-gate/src/gate/report.ts` — Where `renderSummary()` will be added; currently has `renderText()` and `renderJson()`.
+- `packages/frai-gate/src/cli.ts` — Parses `--summary` flag in `cmdCheck()` and routes to `renderSummary()` instead of `renderText()` when present (unless `--json` is also present).
+- `packages/frai-gate/src/gate/validate.test.ts` — Existing test file; new tests for `renderSummary()` will be added here or in a new report.test.ts.
+
+## Tasks & Acceptance
+
+**Execution:**
+- `packages/frai-gate/src/gate/report.ts` -- Add and export `renderSummary(result: GateResult): string` -- Returns a one-liner formatted as `<VERDICT> <answered>/<total>` with block check IDs appended if any blocks exist; handles the special case of missing gate section.
+- `packages/frai-gate/src/cli.ts` -- Add `--summary` flag parsing and output routing in `cmdCheck()` -- When `--summary` is present and `--json` is not, print only the summary line instead of the full report.
+- `packages/frai-gate/src/cli.ts` -- Update HELP text -- Document the `--summary` flag in the check command usage.
+- `packages/frai-gate/src/gate/report.ts` or new test file -- Add unit tests for `renderSummary()` -- Cover all edge cases: all passed, partial blocks, structure missing, warnings only, etc.
+
+**Acceptance Criteria:**
+- Given a GateResult with no findings, when `renderSummary()` is called, then it returns `PASS 7/7`.
+- Given a GateResult with block findings on 'evaluation' and 'transparency' checks, when `renderSummary()` is called, then it returns `BLOCK 5/7: evaluation, transparency` (in GATE_CHECKS order).
+- Given a GateResult with gateSection=null and a 'structure' finding, when `renderSummary()` is called, then it returns `BLOCK 0/7: structure`.
+- Given a GateResult with only warn findings, when `renderSummary()` is called, then it returns `WARN <n>/7` where n is 7 minus the number of warn findings' checks (or all 7 if no blocks).
+- Given the check command with `--summary` flag and a passing spec, when run, then only the summary line is printed and exit code is 0.
+- Given the check command with `--summary` flag and a blocking spec, when run, then only the summary line is printed and exit code is 1.
+- Given the check command with both `--summary` and `--json` flags, when run, then `--json` output is printed (full JSON report), not the summary.
+- The HELP text includes the `--summary` flag in the check command description.
